there is a common belief that true  leaders are born and they are naturally  charismatic influential people destined  to make a mark while we acknowledge that  this fact might hold true for some  people we also strongly believe that  with dedicated efforts it is absolutely  possible to cultivate the traits and  talents required to become a leader so  whether you were born with the  authoritative abilities of captain  america or not if you want to be a  leader you have to work hard to develop  the characteristics of the greats today  in this video we will help you  understand what leadership is all about  along with the personality traits one  should possess to become a leader  but before we begin make sure to  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  that bell icon to never miss an update  from simplylearn  so what do you think leadership is all  about does it have anything to do with  seniority or one's position in a  company's hierarchy if you think yes  then you're on the wrong track of  understanding what leadership is  leadership has nothing to do with titles  management or one's personal agendas  it's also not restricted to personality  traits such as a better vision or  charismatic personality it's more like a  process of social influence which  maximizes the efforts of others towards  the achievement of a common goal  it stems from social influence and  requires human resources to achieve the  intended outcomes  business is a never-ending game  the only way to succeed is to focus on  future growth and how you can get there  and with the help of your human  resources and simply put leadership is  the ability to make that happen moving  ahead let's understand the skills that  you must hone to become a successful  leader  the first skill that you should  emphasize is your ability to listen  listening is an active process and it's  the best way to understand what is  happening in an organization  we frequently find ourselves dwelling on  some other thoughts while having a  conversation as a result we miss out on  critical information or even create a  negative impression at the  communicator's end  so you must enhance your ability to  listen to others  you should develop avenues and channels  for voices to be heard specifically for  those who would not otherwise have the  guts to speak up  you don't always come across solutions  to all problems therefore you must  brainstorm and listen to your team to  bring something unique with each  conversation  next up on our list is clear  communication  communication and trust go hand in hand  no matter how great your ideology and  visions are they will go in vain if you  cannot communicate them to your team  correctly with a proper amount of trust  and confidence  that is why transparency is considered  the foundation of effective  communication  a leader should always be open and  honest about what is known and unknown  he should also ensure that every  listener feels the depth of his vision  with the same level of confidence the  third skill is modeling positive  behavior  when you do what you say you generate  trust and credibility among the people  around you  they will instantly start following and  emulating your actions you can think of  this as an element of leading by example  the ability of a leader to inspire  others through his course of action is  known as role modeling  a leader should also always assist his  followers in staying on the path of  growth  to do this we strongly advise that you  keep track of your team's performance  you should appreciate those who are  doing a good job in order to help them  strive for better performance  on the other hand those that are  underperforming should be steered in the  right direction  next up is resilience and selflessness  resiliency is an important skill in  today's fast-paced and extremely  competitive business world  this personality trait is defined as an  ability to get up faster to bounce back  and reshape after going through a  significant loss or failure being a  leader you should be able to remain  confident and poised in difficult  situations  allow yourself some leeway in dealing  with disappointments  this will help you deal with your  failures fast and learn what else you  could have done better  selflessness is also a critical  leadership personality trait  a leader never elevates himself above  his team  if something does not go right the  leader will always take full  responsibility for it  in contrast if success shows up he will  throw away the credits to his teammates  on that note can you all mention one of  your skills that you think can make you  an effective leader  make sure to drop your answer in the  comments section below let's see how  many of us have what it takes to become  a great leader the last on our list is  effective decision making  leaders in general are those who  question the status quo they are  incredible visionaries change savvy and  agile  every decision they make is not  rudimental and risk-free  they take risks knowing that they'll  need to hold themselves accountable if  things don't work out  that's why to become an effective leader  we advise you to develop the skill of  quantitative decision making  thanks to technology we can now use data  to predict future opportunities and make  sound data-driven decisions that can  take a business to new levels of success  being a leader you should be sincerely  enthusiastic and passionate about your  decisions and actions to fulfill them  this will encourage your team to work  hard towards a common goal with the same  level of dedication and enthusiasm  that's all we have for today i hope this  video is helpful to all of you out there  and i wish you all the very best thank  you for watching the video and stay  tuned for more from simply learn  hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simply learn youtube  channel and click here to watch similar  videos turn it up and get certified  click